Open Canvas Installation Log
=======================

Project Overview:
- TypeScript/Node.js monorepo using Turborepo
- Frontend: Next.js web application
- Backend: LangGraph agents server

Required API Keys:
1. OpenAI API key (https://platform.openai.com/signup/)
2. Anthropic API key (https://console.anthropic.com/)
3. Supabase project URL and anon key (https://supabase.com/dashboard/projects)

Optional API Keys:
1. Google GenAI API key (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
2. Fireworks AI API key (https://fireworks.ai/login)
3. Groq AI API key (https://groq.com)
4. FireCrawl API key (https://firecrawl.dev)
5. ExaSearch API key (https://exa.ai)

Setup Steps:
1. Created Taskfile.yml for common development tasks
2. Created .env files for both web and agents applications
3. Set non-default port 3456 for web application to avoid conflicts

To Run the Application:
1. Install dependencies: `task install`
2. Build the project: `task build`
3. Start both servers: `task dev`
   - Agents server will run on port 54367
   - Web application will run on port 3456

Required Environment Variables:
1. OPENAI_API_KEY - For content generation
2. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY - For reflection
3. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL - For authentication
4. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY - For authentication

Notes:
- The application requires both the agents server and web application to be running
- Authentication is handled through Supabase
- LangGraph server must be running for the application to function properly
- Web application is configured to use port 3456 to avoid conflicts with other local development servers 